## Core Engineering Invariants

Production analytical queries and configurations must adhere to five non-negotiable engineering invariants:

- **Strict Projection Discipline:** Select only required attributes and fields to minimize memory bus traffic and disk reads.
- **Boundary Gating:** Supply explicit, sargable boundary filters in top-level execution predicates.
- **Intermediate Materialization:** Materialize shared, expensive subqueries into temporary structures rather than re-evaluating inline views.
- **Universal Code Style Compliance:** Format all emitted code files using the project formatter with zero permitted formatting diffs.
- **Architectural Naming Standards:** Apply strict structural naming conventions, layer suffixes, and ISO 11179 class words.

